# perl5, target native: a perl of the build host with every core module (Time::Piece for the
# openssl Makefile...), whatever the distribution of the host splits out of its perl package
### It lives in its own prefix, ${GLOBAL_TOOLCHAIN_PATH}/perl5, whose bin directory toolchain.functions
### puts in the PATH of every build, before the perl of the host; setup_full_toolchain builds it before
### the autotools, which record it. The non core modules the builds use are native perlmodule
### recipes installed into it (perl/XML-Parser:native for intltool)
### Plain Configure of the perl sources: no perl-cross, no target dependencies
PKG_DEPS=
PKG_CHECK="[ x$(${GLOBAL_TOOLCHAIN_PATH}/perl5/bin/perl -e 'print $^V' 2>/dev/null || :) == xv${PKG_VER} ]"
